WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.740
- [Narrator] This is the Hercules Beetle,

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.040
one of the largest insects on earth.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.530
The Hercules Beetle is named
for its incredible strength.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.030
It can lift and carry
loads 850 times heavier

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.630
than its own weight.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.998
The most distinguishing characteristic

00:00:21.998 --> 00:00:23.810
of the Hercules Beetle

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.919
is the horn-like pincers on its head.

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:28.719
Only male beetles have
this intimidating feature,

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:31.190
and it is used as a formidable weapon

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.250
in the battle for mating rights.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.999
The horns are usually about
a third of their body length,

00:00:35.999 --> 00:00:38.639
but have been known to grow even longer.

00:00:38.639 --> 00:00:42.039
Hercules Beetles are found
in Central and South America,

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:43.879
and in the West Indies,

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:46.900
and feed predominantly
on rotting wood as larvae,

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.608
and fruit as adults.

00:00:48.608 --> 00:00:51.675
In spite of its strength
and size, the Hercules Beetle

00:00:51.675 --> 00:00:54.500
is a threatened species in many countries.

00:00:56.372 --> 00:00:59.710
Much of its natural habitat
has been lost to deforestation,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.680
and its populations are suffering.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.310
This is the Hercules Beetle.

